    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "runit",
      "text": "runit",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        663.0,
        637.0,
        715.0,
        686.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "informational paragraph",
      "text": "Void Linux is an independent distribution, developed entirely by volunteers.",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        723.0,
        180.0,
        765.0,
        347.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "informational paragraph",
      "text": "Unlike trillions of other existing distros, Void is not a modification of an existing distribution. Void's package manager and build system have been written from scratch.",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        769.0,
        180.0,
        853.0,
        350.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "informational paragraph",
      "text": "Void focuses on stability, rather than on being bleeding-edge. Install once, update routinely and safely.",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        723.0,
        392.0,
        776.0,
        592.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "informational paragraph",
      "text": "Thanks to our continuous build system, new software is built into binary packages as soon as the changes are pushed to the void-packages repository.",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        770.0,
        392.0,
        852.0,
        592.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "informational paragraph",
      "text": "We use runit as the init system and service supervisor.",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        723.0,
        635.0,
        753.0,
        832.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "informational paragraph",
      "text": "runit is a simple and effective approach to initialize the system with reliable service supervision. Refer to the Void Handbook for an introduction.",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        759.0,
        635.0,
        829.0,
        834.0
      ]
    },
